 "about_text": "Tomio Koyama Gallery opened in 1996 in Saga-cho, Koto-ku, Tokyo, and has since become a key platform for Japanese contemporary art. From its earliest years the gallery took part in international art fairs and served as an early point of introduction for young Japanese artists, helping shape a broader current within the country's contemporary art scene. It now operates spaces in Roppongi, Tennoz, Maebashi, and, since November 2024, Kyobashi. The program spans generations and media, representing figures such as Kishio Suga, Hiroshi Sugito, Mika Ninagawa, and Richard Tuttle alongside exhibitions of ceramic artists, reflecting an approach that moves freely across nationality and genre.",
